                <pb facs="0771" n="761" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg761"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.932/7–2248: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-07-22T18:00:00+09:00">July 22, 1948—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 22—8:04 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1347. ReEmbtel 1346, July 22. Foreign Minister has decided Senate reservation
                    cannot be submitted present session Legislative Yuan because Executive Yuan
                    approval, which must be obtained at special meeting, cannot be gotten prior
                    adjournment Legislative Yuan tomorrow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
